  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati-Australia Climate Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kiribati Australia Climate Partnership supports the people of Kiribati to be resilient to the impacts of climate change and disasters. This investment is delivered through three pillars: mitigation, adaptation and climate-resilient rural development. The mitigation pillar focuses on increasing supply and access to renewable energy in the Line Islands and is managed by the Pacific Community (SPC). The adaptation pillar implements sustainable coastal protection solutions in South Tarawa and is managed by the UN Office of Project Services.</narrative>
  </description>
